 Send plain UTF-8 text, not JSON or form fields. For an attachment instead, use `-F 'attachment=@build.log'`. A successful post returns `201` and the new message’s path in `Location`. A blank post returns `422`, an invalid code `401`, and a missing or inaccessible room `404`.
 
-Treat the entire webhook URL as a password. Use HTTPS, mask it in CI output, and redact this route in any proxy access logs or monitoring tools. The Docker image disables Thruster’s unredacted access log by default. Deleting the bot revokes its code without deleting its message history.
+Treat the entire posting URL as a password. Use HTTPS, mask it in CI output, and redact this route in any proxy access logs or monitoring tools. The Docker image disables Thruster’s unredacted access log by default. Deleting the bot revokes its code without deleting its message history.
+
+#### Receiving mentions
+
+Set **Webhook URL** on the bot to receive a JSON `POST` when someone selects the bot from the room’s @-mention list. Use a public HTTP(S) endpoint you control (prefer HTTPS). Campfire delivers callbacks in the background, does not follow redirects, and sends at most one callback per mentioned bot per new message. Clear the field to stop receiving callbacks; the bot can still post with its code.
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "mention",
+  "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/BOT_CODE/messages" },
+  "message": {
+    "id": 118,
+    "body": { "text": "restart the build", "html": "<div>…</div>" },
+    "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`body.text` omits mentions of the receiving bot; `body.html` includes the full rich text. Both paths are relative to your Campfire origin. Keep `reply_to` secret: it includes the bot’s posting credential.
+
+Return `200` with a UTF-8 `text/plain` or `text/html` body (up to 1 MiB) to post a reply immediately. To reply later, return `204 No Content`, then POST to `room.reply_to` using the same format as above.
 
 ### Upgrading
 
